ABSTRACT
This paper introduces the concept of verifiable AI—artificial intelligence systems whose
behavior can be mathematically proven. While all previous AI architectures rely on statistical
guarantees, probabilistic testing, and empirical validation, ST-T1024 is the first AI
architecture designed from the ground up for formal verification.
We present a complete formal specification of the ST-T1024 pipeline in TLA+, demonstrate
the proof of key safety invariants, and show how the architecture's deterministic nature
enables mathematical guarantees of:
· Safety — The system never produces unsafe outputs
· Security — The system has no hidden behaviors or backdoors
· Sovereignty — The system's behavior is fully observable and controllable
· Determinism — Identical inputs always produce identical outputs
· Timing — Worst-case execution time is provably bounded
We further show how verifiability transforms the certification landscape: from "we tested it" to
"here is the proof." This positions ST-T1024 as the first AI architecture capable of Level 3
Trust—trust based on mathematical certainty rather than statistical evidence or vendor
reputation.


